@copilot Update this PR directly rather than opening another PR. Rename only the `version12Test` suite in `instrumentation/aws-lambda/aws-lambda-events-3.11/library/build.gradle.kts` to `core12Test`. The user finds the existing name confusing because this suite varies `aws-lambda-java-core`, not the independently versioned `aws-lambda-java-events` dependency.

Update the suite-specific configuration names, dependency-inheritance wiring, and all references to this particular task, including the representative collection entry in `.github/scripts/instrumentations.sh`, which must become `aws-lambda:aws-lambda-events-3.11:library:core12Test`. Keep the core module's own `version12Test` and the common-events module's `version310Test` unchanged. Preserve dependency versions, isolated baseline/newer-core graphs, shared sources, JVM settings, suite-owned executions, inclusion in `check`, and all current coverage. Do not change production behavior or support minimums, or add a dependency-version metadata label.

Run the narrowest appropriate formatting and validation for the rename. Verify that the events-3.11 baseline and renamed newer-core suites execute tests, including the repository's pinned-latest mode, and that their dependency-inheritance configurations still select the intended versions. Validate the metadata task registration and run the renamed collection task with `-PcollectMetadata=true`, confirming that it still collects `cloud.resource_id` and `cloud.account.id` for scope `io.opentelemetry.aws-lambda-events-3.11`. Keep this a focused naming change and preserve the existing PR's draft state and base.

